<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait credit extension up 2.7 pct in July.</title>
<headline>Kuwait credit extension up 2.7 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic credit extended by Kuwaiti banks rose 2.7 percent to 2.814 billion dinars at the end of July from 2.740 billion at the end of June, Central Bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The credit amounted to 2.112 billion dinars at the end of July 1995.</p>
<p>Balance of cash portion used from domestic credit facilities by sector:</p>
<p>			 Figures in million dinars</p>
<p>					  July '96	    July '95</p>
<p>Trade				     422.4		  641.7</p>
<p>Industry				  238.4		  148.4</p>
<p>Construction			    214.8		  130.0</p>
<p>Agriculture and Fishing		 9.5		    7.6</p>
<p>Non-bank financial</p>
<p> institutions			   141.3		  110.2</p>
<p>Personal Facilities		  1280.9		  602.0</p>
<p>Real Estate			     333.1		  318.5</p>
<p>Other				     173.6		  153.5</p>
<p>Total				    2814.0		 2112.0</p>
<p> of which, consumer loans	   516.2		  542.0</p>
<p>Note: Non-bank financial institutions include insurance, money exchange and investment firms. The figures include the effect of purchasing the debts of Kuwaiti debtors in return for Debt Purchase Bonds since December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.299 dinars)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, Kuwait newsroom 965 -243-1920</p>
</text>
